        "lengths": {},
        "narrative": "<p>THERE APPEARS TO HAVE BEEN GOOD SURVIVAL OF BROOK TROUT STOCKED IN 1988, AND BROOK TROUT STOCKED IN 1987 AND 1986 WERE ALSO SAMPLED. BROOK TROUT GROWTH IS AVERAGE FOR COOK COUNTY. WHITE SUCKER ARE ABUNDANT BUT SMALL, WITH MOST FISH IN THE 6 TO 9 IN SIZE RANGE. GREEN SUNFISH ARE ALSO PRESENT.</p>"
