        "surveySubType": "Population Assessment",
        "narrative": "<p>The catch of brook trout in gill nets was below the normal range for lakes in the Grand Marais area, and was low for this lake, historically.  Three year classes were represented in the catch.  Growth of the brook trout appeared somewhat fast for lakes in the Grand Marais area, and several large brook trout were captured.  Bingshick Lake shows promise as a good place to try for trophy brook trout.As expected, no other game fish were captured.  The catch of white sucker was within the normal range for lakes of this class.</p>",
